From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 07:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: enable MPSS and restore RMTFS

Enable the modem remote processor with the handset firmware path. Restore the
RMTFS region to the high address used by the downstream HD191x device tree and
expected by the modem firmware.

Keep WCN3990 disabled for this first hardware gate. This lets MPSS and RMTFS be
validated independently before the WiFi client is allowed to consume their
services.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts   | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -231,15 +231,20 @@
 };
 
 &remoteproc_mpss {
-	status = "disabled";
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/modem.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &wifi {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/*
+ * Downstream allocates the same high address on every boot. The modem
+ * firmware expects RMTFS there, so describe it statically for mainline.
+ */
 &rmtfs_mem {
-	reg = <0x0 0x89b00000 0x0 0x200000>;
+	reg = <0x0 0xf2901000 0x0 0x200000>;
 };
 
 &adsp_mem {
-- 
2.50.1
